{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273740-book-reference-for-the-need-of-the-changing-breed-animal-part","id":1273740,"title":"Book reference for the need of the Changing Breed animal part.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-10T09:42:58-08:00","id":1273740,"title":"Book reference for the need of the Changing Breed animal part.","content":"I remember that I saw this in some book but I can not remember which one. It's said that without the animal part the changing breed go extinct eventually, like what happened to the Bunyip and Apis. Can someone help me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T10:11:12-08:00","id":1273746,"title":"","content":"All I remember is a sidebar in the Bastet chapter of Changing Breeds. It talks about how the Ceilican could have survived despite their animal kinfolk being extinct. It doesn't really go into detail. There's also some other information about the lost breeds, in their respective chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T19:01:01-08:00","id":1274122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273740-book-reference-for-the-need-of-the-changing-breed-animal-part?p=1273746#post1273746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I remember is a sidebar in the Bastet chapter of Changing Breeds. It talks about how the Ceilican could have survived despite their animal kinfolk being extinct. It doesn't really go into detail. There's also some other information about the lost breeds, in their respective chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the &quot;Extinction and the Cunning Cat&quot; sidebar on p.78 of CB20. In the first paragraph, it specifically states &quot;All Changing Breeds die out when their animal Kinfolk become extinct.&quot; But then it states that that may not exactly be a hard and fast rule and then offers a few possible explanations on how the Ceilican could have survived without their feline Kin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T11:22:50-08:00","id":1274401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273740-book-reference-for-the-need-of-the-changing-breed-animal-part#post1273740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that I saw this in some book but I can not remember which one. It's said that without the animal part the changing breed go extinct eventually, like what happened to the Bunyip and Apis. Can someone help me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember talk of this, maybe in the Changing Breed 20 Book. I think the idea is they will go extinct without them not they all lose their spirit after the last one dies, and more it\u2019s really bad for them to rely off of only homids and they need to find a replacement animal kin to help keep balance.<br /> <br /> Remember the Bubasti are without feline kin right now, but secretly the last khepher cats are bloated Ghouls of the Followers of Set, but eww who wants to breed with that!<br /> <br /> In fact now I want to make a Sorcerer Scientist who wants to research a suitable replacement for the Bubasti tribes feline kin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto"